{"status":"ready","content":"Given the data set: \\(25, 10, 0, 9, -1, -14, -21\\).\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the mean \\(\\bar{x}\\)**\n\n\\[\n\\bar{x} = \\frac{25 + 10 + 0 + 9 + (-1) + (-14) + (-21)}{7}\n= \\frac{25 + 10 + 0 + 9 - 1 - 14 - 21}{7}\n\\]\n\nCalculate the numerator:\n\n\\[\n25 + 10 = 35 \\\\\n35 + 0 = 35 \\\\\n35 + 9 = 44 \\\\\n44 - 1 = 43 \\\\\n43 - 14 = 29 \\\\\n29 - 21 = 8\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\n\\bar{x} = \\frac{8}{7} \\approx 1.142857\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Calculate each squared deviation \\((x_i - \\bar{x})^2\\)**\n\n\\[\n(25 - 1.142857)^2 = (23.857143)^2 \\approx 569.51\n\\]\n\\[\n(10 - 1.142857)^2 = (8.857143)^2 \\approx 78.44\n\\]\n\\[\n(0 - 1.142857)^2 = (-1.142857)^2 \\approx 1.3061\n\\]\n\\[\n(9 - 1.142857)^2 = (7.857143)^2 \\approx 61.71\n\\]\n\\[\n(-1 - 1.142857)^2 = (-2.142857)^2 \\approx 4.59\n\\]\n\\[\n(-14 - 1.142857)^2 = (-15.142857)^2 \\approx 229.31\n\\]\n\\[\n(-21 - 1.142857)^2 = (-22.142857)^2 \\approx 490.30\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the sample variance**\n\nSample variance \\(s^2\\) is:\n\n\\[\ns^2 = \\frac{\\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2}{n-1} = \\frac{569.51 + 78.44 + 1.3061 + 61.71 + 4.59 + 229.31 + 490.30}{6}\n\\]\n\nSum of squared deviations:\n\n\\[\n569.51 + 78.44 = 647.95 \\\\\n647.95 + 1.3061 = 649.2561 \\\\\n649.2561 + 61.71 = 710.9661 \\\\\n710.9661 + 4.59 = 715.5561 \\\\\n715.5561 + 229.31 = 944.8661 \\\\\n944.8661 + 490.30 = 1435.1661\n\\]\n\nDivide by \\(6\\):\n\n\\[\ns^2 = \\frac{1435.1661}{6} \\approx 239.19435\n\\]\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Take the square root to find the sample standard deviation**\n\n\\[\ns = \\sqrt{239.19435} \\approx 15.460\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### Final answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{15.46}\n\\]\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"GPT-4.1 Mini","modelId":"openai/gpt-4.1-mini","promptId":"livebench-065-math","request":{"maxOutputTokens":5000,"reasoning":{"effort":null,"exclude":null}},"response":{"id":"gen-1779371170-yqQGTZZkDPiYaU4TB5Xu","model":"openai/gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14","finishReason":"stop","nativeFinishRea